nt-370432829"},"message":"OK, whoever wrote AutomagicIO... #2255 has abandoned it -- caused to many complaints... I really was trying.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520260504,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQzNzkxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2262#issuecomment-370437919"},"message":"that is ok, I never envisioned AutomagicIO to be used internally where we know what we need to access and when.\n\nRe search: added some logging around the 'query' point:\n```diff\n$\u003e git diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/metadata/search.py b/datalad/metadata/search.py\nindex 84734d37..062ad3eb 100644\n--- a/datalad/metadata/search.py\n+++ b/datalad/metadata/search.py\n@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ import sys\n from six import reraise\n from six import string_types\n from six import PY3\n+from time import time\n \n from datalad import cfg\n from datalad.interface.base import Interface\n@@ -618,8 +619,11 @@ class _EGrepSearch(_Search):\n             # side even for simple queries\n             # DOTALL is needed to handle multiline description fields and such, and still\n             # be able to match content coming for a later field\n+            lgr.log(7, \"Querying %s among %d items\", query, len(doc))\n+            t0 = time()\n             matches = {k: query.search(v.lower())\n                        for k, v in doc.items()}\n+            lgr.log(7, \"Finished querying in %f sec\", time() - t0)\n             # retain what actually matched\n             matches = {k: match.group() for k, match in matches.items() if match}\n             if matches:\n```\nto see that it is a matter of some of those taking way too long (heavier entries, but still...) while others going through super quickly:\n```\n[Level 7] Querying \u003c_sre.SRE_Pattern object at 0x7ffff44fbbe0\u003e among 0 items \n[Level 7] Finished querying in 0.000006 sec \n[Level 7] Querying \u003c_sre.SRE_Pattern object at 0